<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>HTB on Jacob Colvin</title><link>https://jacobcolvin.com/categories/htb/</link><description>Recent content in HTB on Jacob Colvin</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><copyright>&lt;a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;CC BY-NC 4.0&lt;/a&gt;</copyright><lastBuildDate>Sat, 24 Oct 2020 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://jacobcolvin.com/categories/htb/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>HTB Challenge - Reversing - Baby RE</title><link>https://jacobcolvin.com/posts/2020/10/htb-challenge-reversing-baby-re/</link><pubDate>Sat, 24 Oct 2020 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://jacobcolvin.com/posts/2020/10/htb-challenge-reversing-baby-re/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;We can start off by running &lt;a href="https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man1/ltrace.1.html"&gt;ltrace&lt;/a&gt;, which runs a command and intercepts dynamic library &amp;amp; sys calls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;ltrace -i -C ./baby
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We&amp;rsquo;re prompted and can start off by inserting random value, e.g. &lt;code&gt;asd&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A call to &lt;code&gt;strcmp&lt;/code&gt; is intercepted by &lt;code&gt;ltrace&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-c++" data-lang="c++"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;strcmp(&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;asd&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;\n&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;ab[REDACTED]13&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;\n&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Let&amp;rsquo;s start by trying to pass &lt;code&gt;ab[REDACTED]13&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this case it was just that simple, and we receive the flag.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-text" data-lang="text"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;HTB{B[REDACTED]Z}
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;There were probably a lot of additional ways this one could have been solved, and I think I got lucky by starting in this direction.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>